{"codec":"JSON-syntax-dictionary-v4","atoms":["\"identity\"","\"cutoff\"","\"framework\"","\"factor_evidence\"","\"scores\"","\"score_sensitivity\"","\"gates\"","\"history\"","\"historical_vintages\"","\"historical_per_share\"","\"metrics\"","\"incremental_windows\"","\"liquidity\"","\"audit\"","\"sources\"","\"assumptions\"","\"model\"","\"classification\"","\"name\"","\"symbol\"","\"isin\"","\"exchange\"","\"price\"","\"price_date\"","\"shares\"","\"lot\"","\"Quest Laboratories Limited\"","\"QUESTLAB\"","\"INE0TNW01017\"","\"NSE Emerge\"","\"90.20\"","\"2026-10-19\"","16387200","1200","\"2026-10-20\"","\"title\"","\"filename\"","\"sha256\"","\"bytes\"","\"version\"","\"read_in_full\"","\"required_sections\"","\"canonical_factors\"","\"bqs_weights\"","\"gqs_weights\"","\"ias_weights\"","\"Small / Micro-Cap Stock Research Master Prompt v3.0\"","\"Small-Micro-Cap-Stock-Research-Master-Prompt-v3.0.md\"","\"68d4de4255427df276318d0231530b867a453e740c74150e9768bf1387224137\"","72939","\"3.0\"","true","15","13","4","\"GOV\"","\"MOAT\"","\"REV\"","\"DUR\"","\"CAP\"","\"CASH\"","\"BAL\"","\"EXEC\"","\".20\"","\".12\"","\".10\"","\".08\"","\"EARN\"","\".40\"","\".15\"","\"BQS\"","\"R\"","\"D\"","\"P\"","\"L\"","\".25\"","\".35\"","\"factor\"","\"score\"","\"confidence\"","\"rationale\"","\"facts\"","\"strongest_counterevidence\"","\"Medium\"","\"Repeated transparency and stewardship weaknesses, without sufficient evidence to allege diversion or score integrity at 3.\"","\"E01 pp42–49 and E02 p50: inventory assurance limitation persists across two annual reports.\"","\"E01 pp47–48,60,66–68,75: dues, proceeds, equity and related-party tables contain inconsistencies.\"","\"E01 pp67–68: executive remuneration ₹1.32 crore, family salary ₹0.21 crore and controlled-party testing arrangement.\"","\"E12 quashed the historical conviction in April 2026; no current conviction or substantiated fraud may be inferred. No loan default reported in E01 CARO.\"","\"Established formulation capability and tender access, but no proven durable excess economics or pricing power.\"","\"E04 business and risk sections: generic formulations and government procurement dependence.\"","\"E05 slide11: management capacity/utilization claims are not an independently verified cost advantage.\"","\"E08–E11: multiple batch-specific NSQ alerts complicate a qualification-based moat claim.\"","\"Long operating history, six formulation categories and existing government supply relationships provide genuine operating capability.\"","8","\"The preselected five-year nominal reported standalone revenue CAGR falls in the 20% to below 30% bracket; no trajectory adjustment. This is provisional on the declared reported basis, not verified organic demand.\"","\"E04 restated FY21–23; E02 FY24 comparator; E01 FY25–26: no material perimeter change found, but organic constant-scope price/volume bridge is ND.\"","\"Reported growth is 29.7881% over five intervals; three-year growth is shown separately.\"","\"FY26 growth decelerated to 7.56%; one full year alone does not earn an additional trajectory deduction under the chosen policy.\"","\"Inventory and receivable reliability prevent treating this as validated cash-economic growth; G2 excludes ranking. The FY21 low base and subsequent product mix changes reduce extrapolation confidence.\"","5","\"Essential generic-drug demand and existing market access offer runway, constrained by tender concentration, compliance and uncommissioned expansion.\"","\"E04 p39: government sales 61.93% in FY23 and 77.91% in nine months to December 2023.\"","\"E05: FY25 government mix approximately 62.51%, with a minor total-percentage discrepancy.\"","\"E06: Phase I operational September 2026, Phase II machines expected December and trials January–February 2027.\"","\"Injection and export opportunities could broaden products and customers if registrations, qualification and collections are demonstrated.\"","null","\"Low\"","\"NS: audited inventory assurance and vintage/working-capital inconsistencies preclude a defensible sustainable incremental-return score.\"","\"Accounting-proxy ROIC windows are disclosed, not promoted to project returns.\"","\"E01: ₹38.6195 crore inventory, ₹36.2144 crore receivables and ₹1.4604 crore CWIP require economic recoverability evidence.\"","\"Reported operating profit increased materially over five years and the expansion may eventually raise asset utilization.\"","2","\"High on direction; Low on exact disputed amounts\"","\"Persistent poor operating cash realization and aged balances are directly evidenced.\"","\"FY25–26 latest reported CFO totals negative ₹33.9343 crore despite positive PAT.\"","\"E03 original FY24 CFO includes ₹1.630675 crore borrowing proceeds; adjusted conversion is weaker.\"","\"E01 p58: ₹6.5402 crore trade receivables aged two to three years and conflicting over-six-month totals.\"","\"FY26 debt reduced materially and investment disposals funded the cash deficit; this is financing liquidity, not operating conversion.\"","\"NS: actual entry liquidity and undrawn committed facilities cannot be established.\"","\"E01 cash ₹0.1048 crore; ₹10.6469 crore deposits are not assumed unrestricted alongside unspent IPO capex obligations.\"","\"Demand debt ₹6.5336 crore is callable; the financial-risk note repeats outstanding debt as undrawn facilities.\"","\"Actual April–October bank utilization and proceeds bridge are unavailable.\"","\"Reported equity is substantial, debt declined and bank deposits could supply liquidity if availability and restrictions are proven.\"","\"Expansion remains partly unfinished, with delayed IPO utilization and unresolved reporting/compliance weaknesses.\"","\"E01 p75: remaining IPO capex utilization extended through March 2027.\"","\"E06: Phase I operating but Phase II not yet trialed or commissioned at cutoff.\"","\"E05 capacity, daily output and sold-unit claims cannot be reconciled as one physical-capacity model.\"","\"Phase I commissioning is a concrete milestone and reported revenue has increased over the full history.\"","\"NS: operating versus non-operating bridge is calculable, but sustainable per-share profit quality is not established.\"","\"FY26 annual report differs from May results; FY25 comparatives differ from original annual report without a full reconciliation located.\"","\"Inventory valuation directly affects cost and profit; tax benefits and investment income also influence PAT.\"","\"Excluding other income still leaves positive reported operating EBIT, rather than all profit coming from investments.\"","\"NS: no supported five-year equity return can be assigned while actual entry liquidity and financial reliability remain unresolved.\"","\"All modeled paths are explicitly conditional, with no ordinary IRR after a cash-floor breach.\"","\"Optional rescue is bounded and not committed; it cannot cure G3 or supply a supported return score.\"","\"A favorable collection and commissioning path could produce positive returns, but assumptions are not evidence.\"","3","\"Credible inventory/collection loss and recapitalization paths create material permanent-impairment risk.\"","\"₹38.6195 crore inventory lacks auditor verification; ₹6.5402 crore receivables are two to three years old.\"","\"Demand refinancing and capex completion must coexist with very small disclosed cash.\"","\"Bounded financing stress and capital catch-up are explicitly modeled.\"","\"Low reported financial leverage and deposits could cushion a verified adverse scenario; no insolvency is alleged.\"","\"NS: headline P/E is observable but reliable normalized earnings and financeable reverse expectations are not.\"","\"Current price is combined only with clearly dated historical earnings; stale balance-sheet EV is labeled a proxy.\"","\"Reverse-model solutions, if any, remain conditional on liquidity, margins and terminal capital.\"","\"The reported earnings multiple is below 10 times, but this does not validate the earnings or the funding bridge.\"","\"60-session reference arithmetic starts at 5; deduct one point for intermittent trading and material lot granularity.\"","\"Two issuer-absent sessions in validated official archives are conservatively assigned zero capacity, not independently verified zero trades.\"","\"19 October records one trade for one 1,200-share lot.\"","\"₹5 lakh reference position requires four or five whole lots; current spread and full surveillance history are ND. At 5% volume participation, 38 of 60 sessions cannot support a whole lot under the conservative zero-capacity convention.\"","\"The conservative mean/median method gives approximately 7.38 theoretical exit days at 5% participation, not an entirely inactive market.\"","\"GQS\"","\"IAS\"","\"terms\"","\"known_contribution\"","\"coverage\"","\"missing_weight\"","\"raw\"","\"final\"","\"uncapped_lower\"","\"uncapped_upper\"","\"lower\"","\"upper\"","\"caps\"","\"rank_eligible\"","\"display\"","\"weight\"","\"contribution\"","\"0.20\"","\"0.80\"","\"0.12\"","\"0.96\"","\"0.10\"","\"0.50\"","\"0.08\"","\"0.32\"","\"3.58\"","\"3.78\"","\"5.58\"","false","\"0.40\"","\"3.20\"","\"1.00\"","\"0.15\"","\"4.40\"","\"0.70\"","\"0.30\"","\"4.70\"","\"7.40\"","\"5\"","\"Persistent poor cash realization: maximum 5\"","\"0.25\"","\"0.35\"","\"0.60\"","\"1.70\"","\"8.00\"","\"delta\"","-1","\"3.38\"","\"5.38\"","\"3\"","\"GOV <= 3: maximum 3\"","\"Avoid — governance only if adverse facts justify GOV 3; otherwise Research Hold\"","1","\"3.98\"","\"5.78\"","\"id\"","\"status\"","\"reason\"","\"G1\"","\"Conditional\"","\"Material stewardship and disclosure issues; no substantiated diversion and no current conviction inferred.\"","\"G2\"","\"Hold\"","\"Two consecutive inventory assurance limitations and unresolved financial-statement inconsistencies exclude quality rankings.\"","\"G3\"","\"Actual March-to-entry cash and deposit restrictions are unknown; optional rescue is not committed financing.\"","\"G4\"","\"Official lot and 60